{"title":"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa5cd34f4cdaf6f83e81aabe7d567e5fb1871d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=f(x)=\\frac{x+2}{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"37\" />, then it is incorrect to say:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da4b60501b37824ab72d13471a47bf410cd26bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)\\ }x=\\frac{y+2}{y-1}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)\\ }f(0)=-2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)\\ }f(1)=0\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"400\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e5880634d74ad2f6f789df97de59110ba3006e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)\\ }f(-2)=0\\qquad\\textbf{(E)\\ }f(y)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c6a0996509b778dac155e4d9e7e7f72a917ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=\\frac{3}{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />, which is undefined. Hence, the (in)correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f95d31d02794d76d56b19f1fad794494cc53b20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ f(1)=0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"113\" height=\"29\" />.\nWe can verify that the other statements are valid.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/03965ae3cab8e52ce95d75078c8189141e279dc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A).\\ } y=\\frac{x+2}{x-1}\\implies xy-y=x+2\\implies x(y-1)=y+2\\implies x=\\frac{y+2}{y-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"595\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791dac8528246b3e7f7d7ef04a5f03bbb35dbe07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B).\\ } f(0)=\\frac{(0)+2}{(0)-1}=-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"203\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fa2205cc447d7f37a3493ca24a15cd446df6214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D).\\ } f(-2)=\\frac{(-2)+2}{(-2)-1}=\\frac{0}{-3}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"270\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0646a77ef6e7517503811dd41786bf62ffdc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E).\\ } f(y)=\\frac{\\frac{x+2}{x-1}+2}{\\frac{x+2}{x-1}-1}=\\frac{3x}{3}=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"243\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME\" title=\"1952 AHSME\">1952 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1952 AHSME Answer Key\">A